60,3,1,talk,May,,"Option C is the only one that solves my problem. A shared calendar means no more fighting over who got there first, and a booking system implies accountability.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option B would be the most peaceful for those of us sitting by the door. If it's a quiet room, the noise pollution in the office finally stops.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Servas,,Option A would save us the long journey for hot lunches. To nourish the body within our own walls is to preserve the spirit and our time.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"I'm looking at the numbers again! Option C costs 141,000 yen, but it's the only one that stops us from paying those outside hire fees every month!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Option C is the only one that gives us a place for those ""difficult"" conversations. We can't have a ""safe space"" if the room is for sitting alone in silence.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,May,,"@Servas, a kitchen is just a recipe for more crumbs and more cleaning. I'm not voting for a room that just creates more work for the person who cares.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, a meeting space is only a ""safe space"" if the soundproofing is fixed. Otherwise, we're just paying 141,000 yen to let the whole office eavesdrop.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@May, the work of cleaning is a small price to pay for the gift of time and health. A shared meal can mend the fences that a calendar cannot.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"But we can't ignore the budget! If we go with A or B, we're still paying for outside rooms when we need to meet. That's just throwing money away!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, we can make the soundproofing part of the fit-out! If we choose C, we can finally stop being strangers and actually talk to each other.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,May,,"I'm sticking with C. It's the only one with a structure. I can't stand the ""whoever gets there first"" mentality. We need a rulebook.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"I see the logic in C, but I'm worried about the noise. However, if it's the only way to get a proper fit-out that might include a better door or wall...","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Servas,,"I still believe the physical well-being of the staff is paramount. However, I see that the need for a structured meeting space is a strong current here.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Sakura,,Exactly! Let's be professional! Option C is the most logical choice for the company's wallet and our productivity. It's a win-win!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm all for C. It's not just about the money; it's about having a place where we can be human and handle the hard stuff together.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,May,,"Just remember, if we go with C, I'm drafting the cleaning schedule. No exceptions, no excuses. I'm not doing it alone.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"If we agree that the fit-out must address the sound leakage to the office, I can get behind Option C. It's better than the current chaos.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Servas,,It is often the case that the most practical path is the one that leads us to the most harmony. I will support the will of the group.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Sakura,,Yay! I'm so glad we looked at the numbers! It makes the choice so much easier when you see the money flying out the window!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm just happy we're actually talking about this. This conversation itself is a start. Let's make the room a place where we can keep talking.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
